# Both frames carry the NEXT_HOP attribute (40030401020304) beside MP_REACH_NLRI.
# The ExaBGP 6.0 pin (685f772e4) sends the same UPDATE without it, as
# FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF:0048:02:00000031800E20...0A00004001010040020040050400000064,
# observed under --dut exabgp on 2026-10-20. RFC 4760 Section 3: "An UPDATE
# message that carries no NLRI, other than the one encoded in the MP_REACH_NLRI
# attribute, SHOULD NOT carry the NEXT_HOP attribute." Ze keeps it for VPN on
# purpose (family.Family.LegacyNextHop, internal/core/family/family.go), the
# ExaBGP 5.0 bytes api-vpnv4 and the conf-* fixtures pin. Which contract wins is
# the owner's decision; this case pins Ze's bytes, as api-vpnv4 does.
